# clipper (vendored)

Vendored from the PaddleOCR reference distribution (not MNN):
- `clipper.hpp`, `clipper.cpp` from
  `/root/PaddleOCR/deploy/ios_demo/PaddleOCRDemo/ThirdParty/Clipper1/`
  (also available as
  `/root/PaddleOCR/deploy/cpp_infer/...` which uses the same upstream source
  `angusj/clipper` v6.4.2).

This is a Boost-1.0-licensed header + implementation of Angus Johnson's
Clipper polygon clipping/offsetting library. We only use `ClipperOffset` for
the polygon expansion (Paddle's `pyclipper` semantics: `JT_ROUND,
ET_CLOSEDPOLYGON`).

Including the cpp file is the standard way to use Clipper; we link it as a
normal translation unit in our tests/CLI.

See the upstream copyright header at the top of `clipper.hpp` / `clipper.cpp`
for the full Boost-1.0 attribution.
